    {
      "id": "dusk_ives_paid_told",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "“The parish pays one.” He puts the weight down. “Quarterly. Four hundred years of quarters, in the parish book, never missed.” He shrugs. “Ask Fenny Cross who it is. Ask the vicar. Ask Kest, who lives in the hut and is not it. Nobody knows and the money goes.”"
        }
      ],
